# C-Var1/C-Var2: [if cond A B] infers a union of the branch types without error.
#
# The type of an if expression is the union of its two branch types. This test
# verifies that the type checker accepts a function whose return type is
# inferred as Int | Str (from the two branches) without emitting any warning.
# No explicit union annotation is needed — the inferred union type is principal.
#
# C-Var1: the true branch contributes its type to the result union.
# C-Var2: the false branch contributes its type to the result union.
#
# Expected output (populate after CI run):
#   Dict({"choose": Function(flag), "r-true": Int(42), "r-false": String("hello")})
# No === warn section: asserts zero type warnings (union type is accepted silently).
[
  # choose returns Int when flag is true, Str when false.
  # Inferred return type: Int | Str — no annotation required, no warning expected.
  choose: [fn [let flag] [if flag 42 "hello"]]

  r-true:  [choose true]
  r-false: [choose false]
]
=== out
Dict({"choose": Function(flag), "r-true": Int(42), "r-false": String("hello")})
